From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 99993: subscribe to frames on the MLD, so they actually arrive

The agent asks for three frame types per fronthaul BSS - association request,
reassociation request, and action - by the configured interface name. On an MLD
node wifi.ap.<per-link> is published for no BSS, so every one of those requests
fails and the agent receives none of them:

	[wlan0-1] wifi_ubus_subscribe_unsubscribe_frame ret 4
	[wlan1-1] wifi_ubus_subscribe_unsubscribe_frame ret 4
	[wlan2-1] wifi_ubus_subscribe_unsubscribe_frame ret 4

Measured on hardware 2026-08-03. Two consequences, both of which looked like
separate problems until the subscription was traced:

  - A client that associates is not noticed until the next BSS refresh, which
    is once a minute. Measured today: HAL had the client at least 37 s before
    the agent did, and the controller a further 27 s after that. The event that
    should have made this immediate was never subscribed.

  - Action frames carry the BTM Response. Without them the agent never learns
    whether a steer was accepted, so btm_success stays 0 even for a steer the
    client demonstrably obeyed - verified today, client moved between nodes and
    the counter did not move.

Same shape as 9997, 9998, 9999 and 99992: a name that exists per link is used
where the entity is an MLD.

Not fixed here: disassociation is subtype 10 and is not in this subscription
list at all, so a client leaving is still noticed only by the periodic sweep
added in 99991. Making departure immediate needs that frame subscribed too, or
the hostapd event consumed - a separate change, and one that wants its own
measurement rather than being folded in here.

Also unaddressed: the same MLD name is now subscribed once per affiliated link,
so three identical subscriptions per MLD instead of one. Subscribing twice to
the same object is expected to be idempotent; if it turns out not to be, the
guard belongs on mlo_link_id == 0, mirroring the primary-link convention
already used for the master BSSID in bss_stations_data_cb().
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -4630,8 +4630,22 @@
 		strncpy(bss->ssid, fn->ssid, sizeof(bss->ssid) - 1);
 		bss->enabled = fn->enabled;
 
-		for (k = 0; k < num_subfr; k++)
-			wifi_subscribe_frame(f->name, subfr[k].type, subfr[k].stype);
+		for (k = 0; k < num_subfr; k++) {
+			const char *subifname = f->name;
+
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+			/* wifi.ap.<per-link> is published for no BSS on an MLD
+			 * node, so subscribing by the configured name fails
+			 * (ret 4) and the agent never receives the frames it
+			 * asked for: association and reassociation requests,
+			 * and action frames - which is where a BTM Response
+			 * arrives. Subscribe on the MLD entity, as the stats
+			 * and BTM paths already do. */
+			if (fn->is_affiliated_ap && fn->mld_ifname[0])
+				subifname = fn->mld_ifname;
+#endif
+			wifi_subscribe_frame(subifname, subfr[k].type, subfr[k].stype);
+		}
 
 		blob_buf_init(&bb, 0);
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
